                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who, or that which, accumulates."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e8f479e7-9a21-4587-95ca-6ef4927f9042",
                                                "sense_id": "f644a001-bddb-3173-9f91-58a6ea07151c",
                                                "text": "He is a great accumulator of bad jokes."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e5fd87d6-edb5-301e-b365-1ceb0cd29c39",
                                        "entry_id": "89043b55-0623-34db-b0b6-e42a69dca9eb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A wet-cell storage battery."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "British"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d02a205b-7a72-40a6-8501-ac1fb7541471",
                                                "sense_id": "e5fd87d6-edb5-301e-b365-1ceb0cd29c39",
                                                "text": "Looks like it's time to recharge the accumulator again."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9b3bfc42-faef-3bae-861e-d1282bb0e1e2",
                                        "entry_id": "89043b55-0623-34db-b0b6-e42a69dca9eb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A collective bet on successive events, with both stake and winnings being carried forward to accumulate progressively."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c9e34720-e2fa-4d3c-8c02-78178443b1d0",
                                                "sense_id": "9b3bfc42-faef-3bae-861e-d1282bb0e1e2",
                                                "text": "The largest payout for a bet on a horse race was $1,627,084 after tax, paid to Britons Anthony Speelman and Nicholas Cowan on their $64 nine-horse accumulator at Santa Anita Racecourse, California, in 1987."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7ab54f0e-5515-31cc-91c7-92ec8c445eaa",
                                        "entry_id": "89043b55-0623-34db-b0b6-e42a69dca9eb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A system of elastic springs for relieving the strain upon a rope, as in deep-sea dredging."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e1ba3978-7878-3f78-b0d6-7b8282070077",
                                        "entry_id": "89043b55-0623-34db-b0b6-e42a69dca9eb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A vessel containing pressurized hot water ready for release as steam."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4d824da9-b923-3de4-b965-8257b3803877",
                                        "entry_id": "89043b55-0623-34db-b0b6-e42a69dca9eb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A container which stores hydraulic power for release, in the form of a pressurized fluid (often suspended within a larger tank of fluid under pressure)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c048b138-e9d7-37b1-934e-35f7a7e92d61",
                                        "entry_id": "89043b55-0623-34db-b0b6-e42a69dca9eb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A register or variable used for holding the intermediate results of a computation or data transfer."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c21cb298-2d83-4ac3-b2fc-5cd32de51857",
                                                "sense_id": "c048b138-e9d7-37b1-934e-35f7a7e92d61",
                                                "text": "The contents of the memory location and accumulator are NOT altered, but the Negative, Zero and Carry flags are conditioned according to the result of the subtraction."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "90b1edad-7659-43d9-afca-c9f946485a62",
                                                "sense_id": "c048b138-e9d7-37b1-934e-35f7a7e92d61",
                                                "text": "The function signature has changed to include the additional parameter accumulator. This parameter, in a way, takes on the job of the return value."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "645d380c-8b36-3cf3-b4db-ab39b1d64b6b",
                                        "entry_id": "89043b55-0623-34db-b0b6-e42a69dca9eb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A derivative contract under which the seller commits to sell shares of an underlying security at a certain strike price, which the buyer is obligated to buy."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fef29847-0df9-4495-a140-2f482a72f8b6",
                                                "sense_id": "645d380c-8b36-3cf3-b4db-ab39b1d64b6b",
                                                "text": "This product was fairly popular among investors in Hong Kong in 2007 considering the market conditions at that time. It is an accumulator of the underlying stock with a contract period of 12 months."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3b61a652-5ec0-3acf-a690-ce9643199e00",
                                        "entry_id": "89043b55-0623-34db-b0b6-e42a69dca9eb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who takes two higher degrees simultaneously, to reduce their length of study."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK",
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a6651b0e-548c-40d4-9c52-b61d3c12f615",
                                                "sense_id": "3b61a652-5ec0-3acf-a690-ce9643199e00",
                                                "text": "1691–92, Anthony Wood (antiquary), Athenæ Oxonienses\nThe first of these two was a compounder, the other who was an accumulator, was lately made provost of Trin. coll. near Dublin, and on the 31st of March 1692 was nominated bish. of Kilmore."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5a627dbf-de01-30b1-80f2-824215811650",
                                        "entry_id": "89043b55-0623-34db-b0b6-e42a69dca9eb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A one way membership function."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ecfe4754-f450-44dc-b49c-c6596d422b3d",
                        "source_entry_id": "268e5ae3-b0c5-3d24-9331-055ef7df74df",
                        "source_sense_id": "7eba2c9e-7529-35db-bba4-4984d10b63b4",
                        "source_sense_description": "toestel dat de opeenhoping van elektrische lading mogelijk maakt",
                        "target_lang_word": "battery",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "battery",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ded957cf-a041-3627-8b0d-94e50d65507d",
                                        "entry_id": "68ad493e-6279-397c-b990-a4c39c762684",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A device used to power electric devices, consisting of one or more electrically connected electrochemical cells or (archaically) electrostatic cells."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "80a01873-f623-4030-97fc-9594531c10ff",
                                                "sense_id": "ded957cf-a041-3627-8b0d-94e50d65507d",
                                                "text": "lead-acid battery"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "70a3312f-df5a-460f-9728-27b969dc7b6d",
                                                "sense_id": "ded957cf-a041-3627-8b0d-94e50d65507d",
                                                "text": "His flashlight takes two AA batteries."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fd96bf3c-146b-423c-937a-a6b75b98bdcf",
                                                "sense_id": "ded957cf-a041-3627-8b0d-94e50d65507d",
                                                "text": "His car takes a 550-CCA lead-acid battery."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7e66965f-d3ee-432b-9120-1064486760bf",
                                                "sense_id": "ded957cf-a041-3627-8b0d-94e50d65507d",
                                                "text": "alkaline battery"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "55ba848d-c4a5-4dfe-8647-0d2bf7649c83",
                                                "sense_id": "ded957cf-a041-3627-8b0d-94e50d65507d",
                                                "text": "sodium-ion battery"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c6375495-b134-4e6c-a2ef-b31d21fb5148",
                                                "sense_id": "ded957cf-a041-3627-8b0d-94e50d65507d",
                                                "text": "For GMRS [General Mobile Radio Service], rechargeable packs alone do not provide the flexibility that user replaceable batteries can. For instance, once the pack is discharged, it must be placed in the charger and recharged, which can take from one to several hours, leaving you unable to use your radio until the pack is recharged unless you have purchased an extra pack. Extra battery packs are bulky and pricey. With radios using replaceable AA and AAA batteries, you never have to worry about recharging or buying extra packs. You can carry charged replacement batteries in your pocket, purse, or bag, and in an emergency you can even go to a store and buy some alkaline batteries so you can be up and running again."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0896ccd5-c915-3642-bcd1-d959f74b27b8",
                                        "entry_id": "68ad493e-6279-397c-b990-a4c39c762684",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A device used to power electric devices, consisting of one or more electrically connected electrochemical cells or (archaically) electrostatic cells.",
                                            "Such a device that has multiple cells."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "80e14a79-390d-429d-ae23-f1d757b719b8",
                                                "sense_id": "0896ccd5-c915-3642-bcd1-d959f74b27b8",
                                                "text": "Her phone needs a new battery because its present battery no longer holds a charge well."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "297a0ae0-42fa-4ac2-b6a8-2d86bbb9223b",
                                                "sense_id": "0896ccd5-c915-3642-bcd1-d959f74b27b8",
                                                "text": "1749 Benjamin Franklin, letter to Peter Collinson\nUpon this We made what we call’d an Electrical Battery, consisting of eleven Panes of large Sash Glass, arm’d with thin leaden Plates, pasted on each Side...\nA Turky is to be killed for our Dinners by the Electrical Shock; and roasted by the electrical Jack, before a Fire kindled by the Electrified Bottle; when the Healths of all the Famous Electricians in England, France and Germany, are to be drank in Electrified Bumpers, under the Discharge of Guns from the Electrical Battery."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "26ede354-e14c-495b-8f9c-35d24f740a02",
                                                "sense_id": "0896ccd5-c915-3642-bcd1-d959f74b27b8",
                                                "text": "[For his experiments with electricity,] Benjamin Franklin utilized Leyden jars and referred to several jars hooked together as a battery (after a \"battery\" of cannon)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "65e99133-ea82-462b-8ade-ad79110c24a6",
                                                "sense_id": "0896ccd5-c915-3642-bcd1-d959f74b27b8",
                                                "text": "[The voltage of a single cell is] too low for most applications [... so] a series of cells will be used to obtain the desired voltage – a \"battery\" of cells, in the strictest sense of the term."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8f3f0239-2ae8-3932-ba60-683fe71b99c7",
                                        "entry_id": "68ad493e-6279-397c-b990-a4c39c762684",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The energy stored in such a device."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "informal",
                                            "metonymically",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b03b6ba0-31b1-48de-8e05-0b97d334644d",
                                                "sense_id": "8f3f0239-2ae8-3932-ba60-683fe71b99c7",
                                                "text": "Her phone did not have enough battery for another phone call."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ea781678-146f-4170-9925-fa7b6b0fe8b4",
                                                "sense_id": "8f3f0239-2ae8-3932-ba60-683fe71b99c7",
                                                "text": "A: How much battery do you have left? B: Only 63%."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7983469f-3acc-30c0-a9e9-396f6922ab3b",
                                        "entry_id": "68ad493e-6279-397c-b990-a4c39c762684",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The infliction of unlawful physical violence on a person, legally distinguished from assault, which involves the threat of impending violence."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5dcb9109-a13f-455b-b714-e04140a6ebb3",
                                                "sense_id": "7983469f-3acc-30c0-a9e9-396f6922ab3b",
                                                "text": "Holonym: assault and battery"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cd5a1671-1c73-41a1-aad9-825f56fc7e21",
                                                "sense_id": "7983469f-3acc-30c0-a9e9-396f6922ab3b",
                                                "text": "[…] A battery is the actual infliction of unlawful personal violence. […] [The defendant] fell to the ground and lashed out with his feet and in doing so kicked the hand of one of the police officers, fracturing a bone. He was charged with assault […] although this was a battery."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0754ef33-8e6b-48e8-b097-397cb9d44d59",
                                                "sense_id": "7983469f-3acc-30c0-a9e9-396f6922ab3b",
                                                "text": "He offered three types of battery for which Mr. Trump might be liable under New York law: rape, sexual abuse and forcible touching."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4ea1c3c5-2af3-4f41-8153-de43d0d3dd5c",
                                                "sense_id": "7983469f-3acc-30c0-a9e9-396f6922ab3b",
                                                "text": "An order asserted itself, and the hoods on the furnaces were oped wide, and a final march was organized. The wails of the injured and the roars of the dead-on-the-march overwhelmed the tinny speakers in the cell, and they all watched as nearly one thousand people reduced themselves to a few frantic hundred in less than an hour, then settled into a sustained orgy of battery, rapine and rape with no end in sight but the total depopulation of the entire facility."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c35177cf-e46c-31b8-9ef9-d0bb2046597d",
                                        "entry_id": "68ad493e-6279-397c-b990-a4c39c762684",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A coordinated group of artillery weapons, with any of various numbers of guns."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4c136ddb-7487-4a45-a7ea-5aa19f88bb78",
                                                "sense_id": "c35177cf-e46c-31b8-9ef9-d0bb2046597d",
                                                "text": "Outside the ancient fort, you can still see worn areas in the stone where the batteries were once placed."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d81bf9a9-f034-3b44-9689-5b8952359eaa",
                                        "entry_id": "68ad493e-6279-397c-b990-a4c39c762684",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A coordinated group of artillery weapons, with any of various numbers of guns.",
                                            "Such a group of a certain size (number of guns and artillerists), within a schema of military unit organization."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "be98f136-8a48-4140-91f7-bfe6a099fb33",
                                                "sense_id": "d81bf9a9-f034-3b44-9689-5b8952359eaa",
                                                "text": "They sent four batteries southward in an attempt to shore up the defenses around the depot."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "986dec95-d358-4391-84ca-d447cd4585e5",
                                                "sense_id": "d81bf9a9-f034-3b44-9689-5b8952359eaa",
                                                "text": "the marines had six 8-inch howitzers, eight 4.2-inch mortars, and three 105-mm howitzer batteries, each with six pieces."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7d6e06cb-43d8-3461-8aa2-4d2ef875dc02",
                                        "entry_id": "68ad493e-6279-397c-b990-a4c39c762684",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An elevated platform on which cannon could be placed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "countable",
                                            "historical",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "472031c9-5109-4fb7-b727-a043c208afbd",
                                                "sense_id": "7d6e06cb-43d8-3461-8aa2-4d2ef875dc02",
                                                "text": "The construction of advanced batteries mirrored that of those built along the line of circumvallation. [...] Although Mahan demanded that batteries be constructed to exacting dimensions and revetted with gabions, fascines, and sandbags, at Vicksburg the resources at hand determined what materials soldiers used to build what they termed artillery \"forts\"."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bf32b6c1-c941-4231-a3e8-dea493203807",
                                                "sense_id": "7d6e06cb-43d8-3461-8aa2-4d2ef875dc02",
                                                "text": "such forts being so contrived as to have two or three batteries, one higher than the other, furnished with many cannon."
                                            },
